WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.130
I definitely sold. So why hasn't my bank got the money?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.256
Check which pair you sold into.

00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:15.657
If you sold for USDT, you got a USDT balance, not money in the bank.

00:00:15.657 --> 00:00:19.540
Selling and withdrawing to your bank are two separate steps.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:41.269
Same teaching example. You sell 0. 002 bitcoin at 55,000. That's 110.

00:00:41.269 --> 00:00:47.200
Take off an assumed fee of 0. 11, and 109. 89 lands in your account.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.460
So I made ten?

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.805
Take off the costs. Here it's 9.

00:01:10.805 --> 00:01:14.255
79, before any currency conversion or withdrawal fees.

00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:17.770
A price going up isn't the same as your final net gain.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.224
If you need the money back in your bank, first check that your region supports it.

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:43.247
Then convert or withdraw through the official route to an account in your own name.

00:01:43.247 --> 00:01:46.930
Check the name, the amount received, the fees and the processing conditions.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:56.680
No.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.018
Keep your trade and withdrawal records.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.421
If you're not sure what kind of balance it is,

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.720
don't decide based on one 'success' message.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.383
One cheaper network. One wrong click. Your coins may never arrive.

00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:17.450
Next: the checks you never guess.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.890
Understand first, then act.
